.TH PACMAN-UTILS 8 "September 2026" "Parch Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pacman-utils \- Advanced, high-performance Pacman utilities for Parch Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pacman-utils
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pacman-utils
provides a comprehensive suite of C utilities for managing Pacman repositories, caches, package holding, dependency queries, file verification, system health, and mirror ranking.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B edit-sources [\fIFILE\fR]
Safely opens \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR or mirrorlists in \fB$EDITOR\fR with atomic replacement and syntax validation.
.TP
.B repo \fI<list|add|remove|enable|disable>\fR
Manages repository stanzas in \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR.
.TP
.B hold \fI<PACKAGE...>\fR
Adds packages to \fIIgnorePkg\fR in \fI/etc/pacman.conf\fR.
.TP
.B unhold \fI<PACKAGE...>\fR
Removes packages from \fIIgnorePkg\fR.
.TP
.B show-held
Lists all held and ignored packages.
.TP
.B mark \fI<as-explicit|as-dep>\fR \fI<PACKAGE...>\fR
Changes package installation reason.
.TP
.B autoremove [\fI-n, --dry-run\fR] [\fI-y, --yes\fR]
Finds and removes unused orphan packages.
.TP
.B cache \fI<status|clean>\fR [\fI-k <N>\fR] [\fI-u\fR]
Inspects or cleans the package cache in \fI/var/cache/pacman/pkg\fR.
.TP
.B check-updates [\fI-q, --quiet\fR]
Checks for available updates in a non-locking sandbox without requiring root.
.TP
.B why \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Explains why an installed package is present on the system.
.TP
.B deptree [\fI-r\fR] [\fI-d <DEPTH>\fR] \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Displays an ASCII/Unicode dependency tree.
.TP
.B search-file \fI<PATTERN>\fR
Finds which package owns a specific file or library.
.TP
.B history [\fI-n <LIMIT>\fR] [\fIPACKAGE\fR]
Views transactions from \fI/var/log/pacman.log\fR.
.TP
.B top-sizes [\fI-n <LIMIT>\fR]
Lists installed packages sorted by disk footprint.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnoses system health, lock files, broken configs, and partition space.
.TP
.B verify [\fI--all | PACKAGE...\fR]
Verifies file integrity and checks for missing package files.
.TP
.B diff
Interactively manages and merges \fB.pacnew\fR and \fB.pacsave\fR files.
.TP
.B rank-mirrors [\fI-t <TOP>\fR] [\fI-o <OUTPUT>\fR]
Benchmarks mirror download speeds and generates an optimized mirrorlist.
.TP
.B keys \fI<fix|refresh|list|reset>\fR
Manages and repairs the Pacman GPG keyring.
.TP
.B news [\fI-n <LIMIT>\fR]
Fetches recent distribution announcements.

.SH AUTHORS
Written for Parch Linux.
